ta-label pi-secondary-font\">Written by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"illustration\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Illustrated by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"colors\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Colors by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Miquel_Muerto\" title=\"Miquel Muerto\">Miquel Muerto</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"letters\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Lettered by</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/AndWorld_Design\" title=\"AndWorld Design\">AndWorld Design</a></div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"release_date\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Release date</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">June 10, 2020</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<table class=\"pi-horizontal-group\">\n\t<caption class=\"pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-secondary-background pi-item-spacing\">Chronology</caption>\n\t\n\t<thead>\n\t\t<tr>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"previous\">← Previous</th>\n\t\t\n\t\t\t<th class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-label pi-secondary-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\">Next →</th>\n\t\t\n\t\t</tr>\n\t</thead>\n\t\n\t<tbody>\n\t<tr>\n\t\n\t\t<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"previous\"><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_6\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 6\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #6</a></td>\n\t\n\t\t<td class=\"pi-horizontal-group-item pi-data-value pi-font pi-border-color pi-item-spacing\" data-source=\"next\"><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_8\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children 8\"><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #8</a></td>\n\t\n\t</tr>\n\t</tbody>\n</table>\n\n</section>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b><i>Something Is Killing the Children</i> #7</b> is a horror comic from <a href=\"/wiki/James_Tynion_IV\" title=\"James Tynion IV\">James Tynion IV</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Werther_Dell%27Edera\" title=\"Werther Dell&#39;Edera\">Werther Dell'Edera</a> that was published on June 10, 2020 by <a href=\"/wiki/Boom!_Studios\" title=\"Boom! Studios\">Boom! Studios</a>. It is the seventh issue in the <i><a href=\"/wiki/Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_(comic_series)\" title=\"Something Is Killing the Children (comic series)\">Something Is Killing the Children</a></i> comic series, the second issue of the five-part <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_House_of_Slaughter_(comic_arc)\" title=\"The House of Slaughter (comic arc)\">The House of Slaughter</a></i> arc, and the seventh issue of the fifteen-part <i>Archer's Peak</i> saga.\n</p>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Synopsis\">Synopsis</span></h2>\n<blockquote><p><a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a> can never rest. The dust of Archer's Peak has barely settled before the monster hunt takes her to a new town. And in Archer's Peak, life will never be the same; <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a> struggles to put his life back together, while <span class=\"new\" title=\"Tommy (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVG9tbXk/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Tommy</span> begins to think of a life outside the town he was raised in.<sup id=\"cite&#95;ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#91;</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">&#93;</span></a></sup></p></blockquote>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Plot\">Plot</span></h2>\n<p>Mrs. Mahoney and several other parents wait outside the school as bodies are transported to the gymnasium; they will soon be called in to identify bodies. Tommy tells his mother to go home, but she says she won't until she says goodbye to <a href=\"/wiki/Sophie_Mahoney\" title=\"Sophie Mahoney\">Sophie</a>. Inside the school, <a href=\"/wiki/John_Collins\" title=\"John Collins\">Principal Collins</a> takes a drink with <a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Tim Cavanaugh\">Tim Cavanaugh</a>, saying that he feels numb at the horrors they're seeing. Collins asks if they found the animal that did this, and Tim says he's not the one to ask.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a> waits in a tree with <a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a>, who tells her that she knows this won't work. Erica then sees the <span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype children</span> approach, lured out by their mother's body parts. Octo tells Erica that they're crying because she killed their mother, and because they're hungry. Erica then attempts to kill them, but they fade out, uninjured, and escape. <a href=\"/wiki/Aaron_Slaughter\" title=\"Aaron Slaughter\">Aaron Slaughter</a> reminds Erica that <a href=\"/wiki/Oscuratypes\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Oscuratypes\">Oscuratypes</a> are only solid when feeding, but Erica, frustrated that he's here, snaps that she just wanted fewer children to die. She also calls Aaron a brat who doesn't get his hands dirty. Aaron says he knows this breed is personal for her, and then that they're going to need bait to draw out the monsters. Erica refuses to use either <a href=\"/wiki/Bian\" title=\"Bian\">Bian</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/James\" title=\"James\">James</a>, as it means they'll see an Order Ritual and be forcibly recruited. Aaron also references having to take care of <a href=\"/wiki/Tommy_Mahoney\" title=\"Tommy Mahoney\">Tommy Mahoney</a>, reminding Erica that they are not heroes, they are hunters. She quietly agrees to take him to Bian. As they leave, it's revealed that <a href=\"/wiki/John_Richards\" title=\"John Richards\">Officer Richards</a> was still tailing Erica; he tells <a href=\"/wiki/Gail\" title=\"Gail\">Gail</a> to pack a bag for Bian, and that she is not to leave with anybody but him. When Gail says the sheriff won't like that, Richards loads a gun.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Characters\">Characters</span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Order_of_St._George\"><a href=\"/wiki/Order_of_St._George\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Order of St. George\">Order of St. George</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Octo\" title=\"Octo\">Octo</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Aaron_Slaughter\" title=\"Aaron Slaughter\">Aaron Slaughter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Erica_Slaughter\" title=\"Erica Slaughter\">Erica Slaughter</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span id=\"Archer.27s_Peak\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Archer's_Peak\"><a href=\"/wiki/Archer%27s_Peak\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak\">Archer's Peak</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Bian\" title=\"Bian\">Bian</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tim_Cavanaugh\" title=\"Tim Cavanaugh\">Tim Cavanaugh</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/John_Collins\" title=\"John Collins\">Principal John Collins</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Gail\" title=\"Gail\">Gail</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Ms._Mahoney\" title=\"Ms. Mahoney\">Ms. Mahoney</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/Tommy_Mahoney\" title=\"Tommy Mahoney\">Tommy Mahoney</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/John_Richards\" title=\"John Richards\">Officer John Richards</a></li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Monsters\"><a href=\"/wiki/Monster\" title=\"Monster\">Monsters</a></span></h3>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/Oscuratypes\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Oscuratypes\">Oscuratypes</a>\n<ul><li><span class=\"new\" title=\"Archer&#39;s Peak Oscuratype children (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQXJjaGVyJTI3c19QZWFrX09zY3VyYXR5cGVfY2hpbGRyZW4/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Archer's Peak Oscuratype children</span></li></ul></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Comic_guide\">Comic guide</span></h2>\n<table class=\"navbar mw-collapsible mw-collapsed\" data-expandtext=\"Expand\" data-collapsetext=\"Collapse\" width=\"100%\" style=\"border: 1px solid #8c8c8c; background:transparent; border-radius:4px; text-align:center;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"background: var(--theme-sticky-nav-background-color); border-radius:4px;\" align=\"left\"><div style=\"height:3px; margin:0px 0px 0px 3px\"><div style=\"font-size:8pt\"><a href=\"/wiki/Template:Comic_(SIKTC)\" title=\"Template:Comic (SIKTC)\">v</a> • <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"text\" href=\"https://something-is-killing-the-children.fandom.com/wiki/Template_talk:Comic_(SIKTC)\">d</a> • <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" class=\"text\" href=\"https://something-is-killing-the-children.fandom.com/wiki/Template:Comic_(SIKTC)?veaction=editsource\">e</a></div></div> <center><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Something_Is_Killing_the_Children_comics\" title=\"Category:Something Is Killing the Children comics\"><font color=\"#E7F0DF\">Comic guide</font></a></center>\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th style=\"background: var(--theme-sticky-nav-background-color); border-radius:4px;\"><font color=\"#E7F0DF\"><a href=\"/wiki/The_Angel_of_Archer%27s_Peak_(comic_arc)\" title=\"The Angel of Archer&#39;s Peak (comic arc)\">Volume 1: <i>The Angel o